To patch this vulnerability, input validation should be enforced before string interpolation:
```js
const PORT_REGEX = /^\d+$/;
if (!PORT_REGEX.test(String(port))) {
  throw new Error('Invalid port: must consist only of digits');
}
var cmd = `lsof -i:${port}`;
// OR use execFile to avoid shell interpretation entirely:
await cp.execFile('lsof', ['-i', String(port)]);
