The fix involves making the quantifiers deterministic or bounded. For example, changing `\d*[\.]?\d+` to `[+-]?[\d]+(?:\.[\d]+)?` or using atomic groups/cut points (`(?>...)`) ensures the engine commits to a match once it sees digits, completely eliminating the exponential partition search path. This PoC allows maintaining codebases before applying such fixes by verifying that crafted inputs no longer cause CPU spikes or crashes.

