### Why This PoC Demonstrates the Vulnerability

1. **Root Cause Analysis**: The vulnerable regular expression `/^(?:\r|\n)+|(?:\rho|\n)+$/g` attempts to strip leading and trailing newline characters using two separate quantified groups separated by a logical OR (`|`). Because `(?:\r|\n)+` can match either `\r` or `\n` at each position, the regex engine cannot greedily resolve which characters belong to the start versus the end when processing a long string of mixed newlines.
2. **Exponential Backtracking**: When the engine fails to satisfy the `$` anchor (due to trailing non-newline characters or boundary conditions), it backtracks and retries every possible combination of `\r` vs `\n` assignments across both the prefix and suffix groups. This results in `O(2^N)` complexity.
